The rate constant k for the polymerization reaction were determined by the slope of corresponding plots (Fig. 1b) between ln([Mt]/[Mo]) and time. The values of k obtained after linear regression (correlation coefficient r ≥ 0.97) are given in Table 2
                           . The rate constant for 10%, 20%, 30%, 40%, and 50% EHA in the feed were 8.2 × 10−3, 1.2 × 10−2, 1.4 × 10−2, 1.8 × 10−2, and 2.0 × 10−2 min−1, respectively. Where as in case of MMA/BA copolymerization k increased from 7.8 × 10−3 to 1.8 × 10−2 min−1 (Table 3
                           ) by increasing BA from 10 to 50% in the feed.
